A||||12||Sillhouette.com||RSM has finally tested the supercharger on 1/4 mile track||||1||
Z||000000||Sillhouette.com||05-17-2000||10:29 PM||||Today RSM took seven cars to a near by track to see what the engines can do on a 1/4 mile.  The Fiero was in the top beat out a 1998 Z28 with the six speed tranny and a race prepped Fiero  (with nothing in it) the results are :    The Fiero ran 14.3 seconds.  This by itself does not ammount to much however I was told that the track conditions were less than favourable there was some construction around the track and so to compare against other cars the Z28 cam in second with 14.7s.  <P>Your questions or comments are welcome..<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dan86gt3.8||05-18-2000||12:17 AM||||ummmm 14.7 on a ls1??????  I hate to admit it but a stock 6 speed can break into 13's easy, must have ben an awful driver||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sillhouette.com||05-18-2000||01:09 AM||||LS1 I hope you don't mean the V8 engine since that is not what he has in there.  We have finally discovered that the track conditions knocked everyones time off by about a second or second and a half.  Bad driver could have not been the case since the drivers rotated and the best time was actually logged by someone else than the owner.  Look at it this way a camaro could only do 14.7 when a stock one does low 13s.  By this correction factor the fiero is probably in the mid to high 12s.  There will be another race day at RSM towards the fall when the upgrades to the track have been completed.  <P>Later<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||05-18-2000||08:42 AM||||This Fiero that ran 14.3, Was it a stock 2.8 with just the supercharger? Did it has any other modifications? Was using street radial tires or slicks? Which year it was? How much boost?||||reg||1
Z||000004||pollock||05-18-2000||10:14 AM||||A Z28 without a V8?  I don't think so.......<P>If it's a V6 camaro, and the charged Fiero only beat it by that much, i'm pretty disappointed.||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||05-18-2000||11:30 AM||||anyone got air temps?, tires used?, Altitude? I'm sure they were using any kind of engine management systemm... cause for $500 I and Shaun41178 can do better than that... construction? on the track?! or like particulates in the air? sorry for the 20 questions... and a Z28 isn't that fast.. a Z28SS is but no a Z28... they are low 14sec cars... same as Moostang GTs.. Lots of cash for not a really big return. yeah its 1.5-2 seconds better than a stock fiero but still... was that their Rotrex unit? ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Sillhouette.com||05-18-2000||03:00 PM||||Sorry I must have made some error in reading your post. I thought that you meant the fiero has the LS1 in it now I understand you menat that the z28.  Yes the camaro had the LS1 engine in it with larger throttle body and intake system and stainless steel larger exhaust.  The time I gave you is what you can expect for a stock fiero engine.  The actuall time for the RSM engine that is a 3.3 liter overboared and has a crane cram with shorty headers stainless steel exhaust and larger injectors was in the high thirteen.  When I talked to RSM I asked them to give me the times for a stock fiero engine with the supercharger since that is what they sell as a bolt on.   You can expect a half second faster than camaro times on a 2.8 engine with the RSM supercharger on it.  He had 17" rims with cooper tires on it. No slick whatsoever. <BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pollock:<BR><B>A Z28 without a V8?  I don't think so.......<P>If it's a V6 camaro, and the charged Fiero only beat it by that much, i'm pretty disappointed.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||05-18-2000||11:02 PM||||ok ... on 17s i can understand the weak times... my 17s ate up almost half a second! and the DOT slicks helped for about .2-3 tenths... cool.. not a bad gain then.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Shaun41178||05-18-2000||11:41 PM||||Ok I need some clarification on some things here.<P>This Z28 had those mods and it still only ran a best of a 14.7?  Like you said there were different drivers but there is no way in hell that it should run that slow with those mods.  Sure you could have had drivers rotating but if they all can't shift worth a darn then it doesnt' mean anythign to put different drivers in.  They are high 13 second stock easy.  What elevation you gys at?  You in the Damn mountains?  RSM being near Toronto I doubt the elevation is more then 1000 feet which I suspect is where the test track was close to.  That Camaro is off by about 1.5 seconds or so but that 2.8 with the supercharger kit at a 14.3 sounds correct to me.  That 2.8 with the supercharger wont' come close to a 12.  According to the dyno printout it has 200 hp but at like 100 mph.  thats just not enough power to get it into the 12's<P>The Fiero had 17 inch rims or the camaro had 17 inch rims?  17 on Camaro are stock.  What were the 60 foot times of the Fiero and Camaro?  This will tell a lot if the Camaro has like a 2.5 or so as that would mean it was spinning which would be the reason for the cause of a high Et.  What about 1/8 mile times?  Those on the timeslips?<P>The RSM with the 3.3 liter, did it have a supercharger too?  if so you said it was only running a high 13, thats pretty bad.  The 3.3 should be a 12 second car.  If not then a high 13 sounds right to me.  What were the 60 foot and 1/8 mile numbers of this 3.3 Fiero?<P>Oh yea how much boost on this 2.8 with the kit?<P>Shaun||||reg||1
Z||000009||Dan86gt3.8||05-19-2000||02:39 PM||||well from my experiences and what I have seen all the ls1's run the same it doesen't matter if it's a z28, ss, ws6, or a vette they still run right in the same range.  I was also at a strip about a month or 2 ago and some yahoo had the famed ss and couldn't even get into the 13's, the reason for this is most likely because everytime he shifted the front end would dip back down for about a second then raise back up, it was really noticeable on 1-2 then almost as bad on 2-3.  This means he defenitely wasn't powershifting, or even speed shifting for that matter.  With a really good driver and perfect conditions (ie englishtown, Baytown in houston) they can run low 13's.  the cars are very impressive if a: they have a good driver and b:hook up well.  defenitely the fastest from the factory cars around right now.  I wish I had thier engine in my fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Sillhouette.com||05-20-2000||09:04 AM||||I'll try to answer your questions.  There were three fieros there. One was the 3.3 with the supercharger and the other two only had a 2.8 with custom pistons crane cam roller rockers shaved heads larger throttle body and so on.  All this was present on the 3.3 as well plus the supercharger.  The reason for the bad track time is because of track conditions.  There was a lot of rubber on the track one could barely walk withoug sinking into the molten rubber. The camaro has 300 hp right now the supercharged fiero has 250 hp but the weight difference is a big deal.  About your number questions I'll do a better tell me how to post time slips on here and I'll post the slips. Now there were about 13 runs from each car.  Which one do you want and which car.  Here are the cars of importance.  <P>Fiero 3.3 supercharged (10psi)<BR>Fiero 2.8 race prepped done up engine but taken out interior and a lot of weight reduction<BR>Fiero 2.8 with stock interior 4 speed<BR>Camaro Z28 with all the option available including the LT1 Engine and six speed tranny.<P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000011||GT Bastard||05-20-2000||11:58 AM||||Stock Camaro rims are 16', not 17'.  Maybe the SS has 17' as an option, but not stock.  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Dan86gt3.8||05-21-2000||11:55 PM||||ok I didn't knoiw we were talking about an lt1 here.  You said it was a 98 that means an ls1, but you said it had an lt1, big difference there, an lt1 is still a good motor, just needs a little prompting to come alive.||||reg||1
